# Flight Logbook

> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.
> Newest entries first. One block per insight.

## 2026-09-23

### TASK-260922-vcx6yo — rev1 rework: overlap axes and isolated M2/M5 kills

- P1 CLOSED (read-only atomicity): added `TestAttachReadOnlyOverlapAdmissionAtomicAcrossLifecycleInstances`. It pauses the first receipt after staging, races a second read-only client through an independent Lifecycle/store, and asserts one receipt/vector. `N-M2-attach-admission-lock-input-only` was run alone; it KILLED and the raw log shows the second receipt and read-only vector were returned.
- P2 CLOSED (input peer position): added `TestAttachOverlapInputGateChecksEveryPeer` for a read-only peer sorting before one input peer and before two input peers. Each refusal asserts no new receipt and no vector. `N-M5-attach-overlap-input-first-peer-only` was run alone; both subtests KILLED with receipt/vector effects in the raw log.
- Added `TestAttachOverlapRequiresMultiAttachForInputClient`; its separate `N-attach-overlap-multi-input-client` narrowing isolates `multi_attach` by keeping `multiple_input_clients` present. Expanded `TestAttachReceiptWithoutPositiveLivenessRemainsPossiblePeer` to cover read-only and input-authorized receipts whose returned vectors have not been executed.
- Gate-axis census is complete across client class, peer count, sorted peer position, replay/new client, and concurrent/sequential calls: 6 gates × 5 axes = 30 rows, with 15 test-and-narrowing witnesses and 15 owned bounds. M2/M5 each have a single-killer raw log. The refreshed results, matrix, validation logs, and evidence archive are ready for review.
- Focused axis tests and the `termbind` + `tmuxserver` package suite passed on the current candidate. Candidate remains uncommitted on Story checkpoint `d8decbb03db419c8ad2707cadc2eafd3027a9c4d`.

### TASK-260922-vcx6yo — attach overlap admission, atomic census, and liveness bound

- P1 FIXED (overlap capability gates): `Lifecycle.Execute(attach)` now keeps the landed `AttachStore.Peers` census as the single receipt-namespace authority, then requires `multi_attach` for a distinct possible peer and `multiple_input_clients` plus valid AX input authorization for concurrent input. Receipt-validated same-client retries are distinguished from new clients. The read-only-no-multi and writable-no-multiple-input paths refuse before a second receipt or vector; peer-present read-only/input retries and conflicting retries are exercised at the lifecycle entry.
- P1 FIXED (attach-to-attach atomicity): a persistent per-instance OS lock spans the peer census through receipt installation. Unix uses `flock`; Windows uses `LockFileEx`. A paused receipt-stage interleaving across independently constructed Lifecycle values proves the second attach cannot commit from an empty census; separate-store and killed-process tests prove contention, cancellation, and kernel release. Existing quiesce ordering remains process-local under B42.
- LIVENESS RULE / B44: a receipt proves an admitted client claim, not current tmux connectivity. The returned vector is caller-executed and this protocol has no positive client-identity or detach signal. If liveness cannot be shown, it is UNKNOWN and remains a possible peer; that can conservatively block a later attach after detach. Exact liveness and stale-receipt reclamation stay owned by a future authoritative protocol/receipt owner. The landed census remains fail-closed for corrupt, unreadable, directory-shaped, misfiled, and foreign-keyed entries; no second census was added.
- OUTCOME COMPOSITION: the 216-row base/candidate closure grid shares all 216 `(package, entry, input)` keys. One outcome moved: `tmuxserver | ExecuteAttachOverlapRace | two-writable-clients/no-multiple-input-clients` now refuses the second attach with `terminal_backend_capability_unproven`, commits no second receipt, and returns no vector. All 33 importer packages have outcome rows; the accepted closure's three package-surface bounds (`cloneproject`, `crashgate`, `sshtransport`) remain explicitly fenced and their package tests ran.
- MUTATION / VALIDATION: the initial candidate harness had 301 rows; that evidence is superseded by the rev1 review-rework pass recorded above. The refreshed tmuxserver harness has 304 unique rows (297 narrowing and 5 supplementary KILLED; one shadowed supplementary and C-control SURVIVED). All 45 Go packages passed regular, race, and coverage sweeps; all 17 configured 100x fuzz targets, Linux and Windows builds, native/Windows vet, tracecheck, cataloggen, importer package tests, JSON parsing, and formatting checks passed. `task-board validate` exited 0 and reported 254 unrelated task issues; none named this task or its Story.
- PROCESS ANOMALY: an earlier path typo briefly created `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/internal/termbind/admission_test.go` outside this Story worktree at `2026-09-23T05:25:21+0400`. It was removed immediately; the removal timestamp was not captured, and a final presence check confirms the file is absent. No direct control-root edit was made.
- Candidate remains uncommitted in the Story worktree at checkpoint `d8decbb03db419c8ad2707cadc2eafd3027a9c4d`.

## 2026-09-22

### TASK-260830-1c28dz rev9 — census integrity, in-flight probe bounds, validated replay, attribution repair

- P1 FIXED (receipt-namespace directory fails closed): the peer census skipped every directory before reading, so a directory at the exact `<client-UUID>.json` receipt path read as no peers and admitted a second client without `multi_attach`. The census now skips only staging (`attach-*`) and non-receipt names; any other entry — including a directory — must read as a valid receipt file or the attach refuses. Narrowings `N-attach-peers-dir` (termbind) and `N-attach-peers-dir-skip` (tmuxserver, cross-package plant) KILLED through the census test and the entry test; new census row peershape.
- P2-A FIXED (read-only probes honor the deadline in-flight): the stop poll, the terminate-stale self-confirm, and the status live probes ran under the caller's context while the deadline lived only in a field/clock checks, so a blocked probe waited past the bound. One shared `probeContext` (duration-derived, fake-clock-safe: answered probes follow the clock exactly, only never-answered probes conclude by the context) now bounds all three; expiry concludes unknown, never a verdict. Release-controlled entry tests pin refusal-before-release with no kill/closure/termination/report. Shared narrowing `N-probe-deadline` KILLED through all three entries with isolated single-test attribution. Runner audit: every other wait/probe is deadline-bounded (barrier/admission/boundary/dial); single-shot commits stay caller-cancellation-bounded as stated bound B45 (engine-mirrored; a hung commit hangs, never mis-verdicts).
- P2-B NARROWED (receipt-validated replay with a peer present): the overlap gate demanded overlap capabilities before consulting the durable store, so an identical same-client retry with another peer present refused `capability_unproven`. A Lookup-proven recorded receipt now exempts the retry (replay, or `idempotency_mismatch` when transport/input changed, after the live authorization recheck); a client with no recorded receipt still gates however it names itself. Pin: input + read-only replay shapes with an input peer, plus the conflicting-retry mismatch leg. Narrowing `N-attach-overlap-replay-unproven` KILLED; census row overlapreplay; B44 clarified (validated replay here, liveness with TASK-260922-vcx6yo).
- P2-D REPAIRED (isolated kill attribution): the three shared escalation/wait plants claimed per-entry kills the fixtures could not deliver (quiesce auth subtest at exact expiry under the -1h plant; strictly-past deadline case vs the equal-instant narrowing; boundary-commit 7h advance vs the +1h widening). Fixtures now drive the admitted class (30-min-past expiry, on-deadline instant leg, 6.5h advance with release-controlled barrier) and every shared plant kills through every claimed killer ALONE, twice, with the companion/precision legs green — stop 4 / quiesce 4 and 4 wait killers measured, not claimed. Census: 148 gates, 266 measured of 5504 (pollbound measured; terminate tail corrected U1→B39); battery 296/296 + 42/42.
- P2-C REPAIRED (evidence freshness): the rev9 evidence archive is built from the frozen rev9 tree and attached with its absolute path, then read back and digest-verified from the board — the stale-archive failure is closed by construction, not by prose.

