### TASK-260922-vcx6yo — attach overlap admission, atomic census, and liveness bound

- P1 FIXED (overlap capability gates): `Lifecycle.Execute(attach)` now keeps the landed `AttachStore.Peers` census as the single receipt-namespace authority, then requires `multi_attach` for a distinct possible peer and `multiple_input_clients` plus valid AX input authorization for concurrent input. Receipt-validated same-client retries are distinguished from new clients. The read-only-no-multi and writable-no-multiple-input paths refuse before a second receipt or vector; peer-present read-only/input retries and conflicting retries are exercised at the lifecycle entry.
- P1 FIXED (attach-to-attach atomicity): a persistent per-instance OS lock spans the peer census through receipt installation. Unix uses `flock`; Windows uses `LockFileEx`. A paused receipt-stage interleaving across independently constructed Lifecycle values proves the second attach cannot commit from an empty census; separate-store and killed-process tests prove contention, cancellation, and kernel release. Existing quiesce ordering remains process-local under B42.
