HEAD:.task-board/EPIC-260903-235vty_cross-machine-swarm-coordination/STORY-260903-i05b8l_landing-reaches-trunk-and-is-visible/TASK-260903-2e8rws_computed-commit-time-policy/README.md:14:1. New sidecar key `version_control.commit_time_policy`, validated by `pkg/remoteconfig` like every other sidecar key (duplicate keys refused, unknown kinds refused). Shapes: `{'kind': 'now'}`; `{'kind': 'previous_day_at', 'time': 'HH:MM', 'timezone': '<IANA zone>'}`. `previous_day_at` resolves to the calendar day before the landing's wall-clock date in the given zone, at the given time, with that zone's offset, formatted RFC3339. This repository's policy is expressed as `{'kind': 'previous_day_at', 'time': '20:01', 'timezone': 'Europe/Moscow'}`; changing this repository's `task-board.config.json` to add that key is part of this task's delivery and is the only configuration change in the wave.
HEAD:.task-board/EPIC-260903-235vty_cross-machine-swarm-coordination/STORY-260903-i05b8l_landing-reaches-trunk-and-is-visible/TASK-260903-2e8rws_computed-commit-time-policy/README.md:15:2. `worktree integrate` and `worktree checkpoint` (trunk `cmd/worktree_checkpoint.go`, which after PR #131 makes no board transition and no longer carries `checkpointVersionControlPolicy()` into a `done` transition; the policy read must move to the commit path) resolve the commit time in this order: an explicit `--commit-time` flag (unchanged, manual resume path); else `commit_time_policy` when configured; else, when `confirm=false`, the current time; else refuse `commit_time_policy_unconfigured` BEFORE the transaction opens, with a packet naming the config key. The automatic path (TASK-260903-2xw0ar (acceptance-lands)) never passes the flag, so the refusal maps to `blocked` there. The tool never asks and never guesses, and an unreadable or malformed `version_control` sidecar is a refusal (`config_unreadable`, naming the file), never 'no policy'.
HEAD:.task-board/EPIC-260903-235vty_cross-machine-swarm-coordination/STORY-260903-i05b8l_landing-reaches-trunk-and-is-visible/TASK-260903-2e8rws_computed-commit-time-policy/README.md:18:5. `project_config()` exposes `version_control.commit_time_policy` in its `version_control` projection next to the existing `confirm` and `desired_commit_time` fields (see `references/querying.md`).
HEAD:.task-board/EPIC-260903-235vty_cross-machine-swarm-coordination/STORY-260903-i05b8l_landing-reaches-trunk-and-is-visible/TASK-260903-2e8rws_computed-commit-time-policy/README.md:40:1. `version_control.commit_time_policy` with kinds `now` and `previous_day_at` is accepted by sidecar validation; an unknown kind, a malformed `time`, an unknown IANA `timezone`, or `previous_day_at` without `time`/`timezone` is refused with a typed config error naming the dotted key. A duplicate `commit_time_policy` key is refused by the existing duplicate-key scan.
HEAD:.task-board/EPIC-260903-235vty_cross-machine-swarm-coordination/STORY-260903-i05b8l_landing-reaches-trunk-and-is-visible/TASK-260903-2e8rws_computed-commit-time-policy/README.md:42:3. `worktree integrate` and `worktree checkpoint` with `confirm=true`, no `--commit-time` and no policy refuse `commit_time_policy_unconfigured` before the transaction opens and move no ref; the same commands with the policy configured create commits whose author and committer dates equal the computed time (asserted with `git log --format=%aI/%cI`); an explicit `--commit-time` still wins. A mutant that falls back to `now` when `confirm=true` and no policy exists fails the suite; a NARROWING mutant that applies the policy to the author date only fails on the `%cI` assertion; the production call sites are named (`changerequest.Checkpoint`'s commit-tree call and the integrate session's commit step).
HEAD:.task-board/EPIC-260903-235vty_cross-machine-swarm-coordination/STORY-260903-i05b8l_landing-reaches-trunk-and-is-visible/TASK-260903-2e8rws_computed-commit-time-policy/progress.md:22:- [x] Add version_control.commit_time_policy to the sidecar schema with kinds now and previous_day_at, typed refusals for malformed shapes, and duplicate-key coverage
HEAD:.task-board/EPIC-260903-235vty_cross-machine-swarm-coordination/STORY-260903-i05b8l_landing-reaches-trunk-and-is-visible/TASK-260903-2e8rws_computed-commit-time-policy/progress.md:24:- [x] Wire the resolution order (flag, policy, now-when-confirm-false, otherwise refuse commit_time_policy_unconfigured before the transaction opens) into integrate and checkpoint
HEAD:.task-board/EPIC-260909-1d85k3_incident-management-and-register/STORY-260917-1ylyl3_ax-orchestration-incident-review-260917/BUG-260923-2ek2ca_runner-story-final-landing-cannot-satisfy-version-control-confirm/README.md:6:Since BUG-260915-3l1ftu the runner lands story_final integration runs by re-entering worktree integrate without --commit-time; with version_control.confirm=true every runner landing refuses integration_blocked, and the runtime Integration Assignment forbids the agent from running integrate itself, so no route lands a story_final CR. Observed in agent-session-manager 2026-09-23 (RUN-260923-71a721, RUN-260923-3de6a0). Fix: the integrate slice of TASK-260903-2e8rws: version_control.commit_time_policy (now | previous_day_at) validated by pkg/remoteconfig and resolved by worktree integrate and the board commit in the order flag, policy, now-when-confirm-off, else refuse before the transaction opens.
HEAD:.task-board/EPIC-260909-1d85k3_incident-management-and-register/STORY-260917-1ylyl3_ax-orchestration-incident-review-260917/BUG-260923-2ek2ca_runner-story-final-landing-cannot-satisfy-version-control-confirm/README.md:12:1. version_control.commit_time_policy kinds now and previous_day_at accepted; unknown kind, malformed time, unknown IANA zone, or previous_day_at missing time/timezone refused naming the dotted key. 2. worktree integrate and worktree complete resolve flag > policy > now(confirm off) > refuse commit_time_policy_unconfigured before any transaction or ref moves; with confirm on and a policy configured an integrate without --commit-time (the runner landing) proceeds with the policy time, recorded with its source in the transaction and result. 3. previous_day_at resolves to the previous calendar day in the zone at HH:MM with that zone offset, DST-correct. 4. The runner landing refusal leads with the refusing line and classifies commit_time_policy_unconfigured, not the warn-policy write-boundary report. 5. Narrowing tests: removing the policy arm, treating confirm-without-policy as now, dropping the classifier code and the headline reorder each redden a named test. Out of scope (TASK-260903-2e8rws): worktree checkpoint and board commit.
HEAD:.task-board/EPIC-260909-1d85k3_incident-management-and-register/STORY-260917-1ylyl3_ax-orchestration-incident-review-260917/BUG-260923-2ek2ca_runner-story-final-landing-cannot-satisfy-version-control-confirm/progress.md:24:Landed PR #356 as 66dbad67 (exact-head comment review, hosted test pass 1h14m, plain ff cef15c93..66dbad67). Integrate slice of TASK-260903-2e8rws: version_control.commit_time_policy (now|previous_day_at), integrate/complete resolve flag>policy>now(confirm off)>refuse commit_time_policy_unconfigured before any txn; runner refusal headline leads with the refusing line. 4/4 narrowing mutants killed + control. checkpoint and board commit remain with 2e8rws. Installed via curator global install (task-board build 5bb42957). Consumer: agent-session-manager PR #60 sets commit_time_policy {kind: now}.
