### Inherited handoffs also closed

- Read-only to writable escalation: TestExecuteAttachReadOnlyReceiptCannotEscalateToWritable drives Lifecycle.Execute. It asserts literal idempotency_mismatch, no vector, and no receipt mutation. N-attach-readonly-to-writable weakens the landed store refusal and the behavior test fails.
- Foreground composition: TestForegroundAcquireComposesProductionProbeWithAttach drives the real Production probe through foreground Acquire and Lifecycle.Execute(attach) with a private live Unix socket. No tmux process starts.
- Fresh-decoy foreground wiring: TestAcquireForegroundRefusesEveryCatalogDecoyRunning drives foreground Acquire. N-foreground-fresh-decoy-wiring admits only a fresh headless_creation decoy and is killed by the production-entry test.

No new capability is advertised. The tests use a real Unix socket fixture but do not launch tmux. B44 remains an explicit liveness bound owned by a future authoritative receipt/protocol owner: an attach receipt is not positive evidence that the client remains connected.

