.temp/TASK-260830-g0pcnt/LOGBOOK.stage3.md:32:- P2-B NARROWED (receipt-validated replay with a peer present): the overlap gate demanded overlap capabilities before consulting the durable store, so an identical same-client retry with another peer present refused `capability_unproven`. A Lookup-proven recorded receipt now exempts the retry (replay, or `idempotency_mismatch` when transport/input changed, after the live authorization recheck); a client with no recorded receipt still gates however it names itself. Pin: input + read-only replay shapes with an input peer, plus the conflicting-retry mismatch leg. Narrowing `N-attach-overlap-replay-unproven` KILLED; census row overlapreplay; B44 clarified (validated replay here, liveness with TASK-260922-vcx6yo).
.temp/TASK-260830-g0pcnt/LOGBOOK.stage3.md:36:### TASK-260830-1c28dz rev8 — post-wait revalidation, bounded waits, overlap fail-closed
.temp/TASK-260830-g0pcnt/LOGBOOK.stage3.md:40:- P1-B NARROWED (overlap fail-closed): this leaf has no liveness census, so a stored peer receipt reads as possibly live — a second client needs `multi_attach`, new input over an input peer needs `multiple_input_clients`, same-client retries exempt, unreadable peers fail closed. Over-strict by design (detached clients' receipts still trigger) until the liveness census lands; owner TASK-260922-vcx6yo, stated as B44. Narrowings `N-attach-overlap-multi` / `-input` KILLED with two-peer precision legs. The §4.C attach row claims only the fail-closed gate, never liveness.
