nceIdentity'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['terminal-instance-identity-exact'], 'coverage': 'sliver', 'gap': 'CheckInstanceIdentity enforces Section 4.B clause 4.B#11 (terminal instance identity is never a PID, handle, socket, path, pipe, URL, token, or endpoint) across the Binding, operation bodies, bootstrap binding, and attach surfaces; the Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 closed object itself is parsed by ParseTerminalBinding with ID recompute (terminal-instance-binding-exact covers the unmeasured table rules). The other 11 Section 4.B clauses (Manifest/Probe/evidence reconciliation rules, reader ID recompute, generation boundary cases) are implemented in internal/terminalbackend Reconcile/AdmitProbe and stay unenumerated here.', 'clauses': [{'id': '4.B#11', 'line': 1076, 'excerpt': 'Identity MUST NOT be a PID, handle, socket, path, named pipe, URL, token, or', 'acceptance_cases': ['terminal-instance-identity-exact']}]}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:1.6'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/scalar/scalar.go', 'declaration': 'ErrInvalidScalar'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['scalar-uuid-validation', 'scalar-timestamp-validation', 'scalar-digest-validation', 'scalar-platform-provider-validation', 'scalar-provider-id-validation', 'scalar-relative-path-validation', 'scalar-absolute-path-validation', 'scalar-bounded-integer-validation', 'scalar-decimal-uint64-validation', 'scalar-closed-enum-validation', 'canonical-jcs-rfc8785', 'canonical-object-identity', 'canonical-identity-refusal'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': 'ErrInvalidScalar is the internal/scalar refusal funnel for the common wire scalars Section 1.6 declares, but its CBOR decoder clauses, its UTF-16 ordering derivation clause and its wall-clock-ownership clause have no implementation, and no clause of Section 1.6 is enumerated against an acceptance case.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:2.1'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/canonicaljson/closed_shapes.go', 'declaration': 'validateSessionRecordCommon'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['canonical-object-identity', 'canonical-identity-refusal'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': 'The single Section 2.1 clause is a replica runtime obligation - no run or resume of the logical session without takeover or fork - and validateSessionRecordCommon only validates Session Record shape, so nothing in this binding discharges it.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:2.3'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/canonicaljson/closed_shapes.go', 'declaration': 'validateSessionRecordCommon'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['canonical-object-identity', 'canonical-identity-refusal'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': 'validateSessionRecordCommon validates the immutable Section 2.3 name grammar only; local/peer lookup, ASCII-fold collision handling, route choice and the associated runtime errors are not implemented, and no clause of Section 2.3 is enumerated.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:2.4'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/sessprofile/authority.go', 'declaration': 'Derive'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['sessprofile-derive', 'sessprofile-derive-heads', 'sessprofile-fork-pair', 'provhost-mapping-resolution', 'story-260917-losing-lease-profile-source', 'story-260922-derivation-side-profile-source'], 'coverage': 'full', 'clauses': [{'id': '2.4#1', 'line': 661, 'excerpt': 'MUST fail with <code>profile_mapping_unavailable</code> if the adapter cannot map the stored profile for the probed provider version.', 'acceptance_cases': ['provhost-mapping-resolution']}, {'id': '2.4#2', 'line': 666, 'excerpt': 'Losing-lease or ambiguous events MUST NOT change it.', 'acceptance_cases': ['sessprofile-derive', 'story-260917-losing-lease-profile-source', 'story-260922-derivation-side-profile-source']}, {'id': '2.4#3', 'line': 670, 'excerpt': 'a bundle, resume, or fork MUST NOT fall back to the Session Record creation value when the closure contains a later change.', 'acceptance_cases': ['sessprofile-derive', 'sessprofile-derive-heads']}, {'id': '2.4#4', 'line': 678, 'excerpt': "MUST NOT be treated as a profile event in the new session's event chain.", 'acceptance_cases': ['sessprofile-fork-pair']}]}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:6.1'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/config/loader.go', 'declaration': 'Load'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['config-versioned-readers'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': 'Load resolves and reads the Section 6.1 configuration roots, but the clause requiring those resolved roots across the CLI, service, RPC server and provider host has no implementation, and no clause of Section 6.1 is enumerated.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:6.2'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/config/schema.go', 'declaration': 'Decode'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['config-versioned-readers'], 'coverage': 'full', 'clauses': [{'id': '6.2#1', 'line': 2512, 'excerpt': 'MUST be <code>conpty</code>. WSL2 configuration uses Linux paths and <code>platform = "wsl2"</code>.', 'acceptance_cases': ['config-versioned-readers']}]}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:6.3'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/config/validation.go', 'declaration': 'validateConfiguration'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['config-versioned-readers', 'config-current-writer'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': 'validateConfiguration enforces many Section 6.3 field constraints, but no clause of Section 6.3 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about its obligations.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:6.4'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/config/migration.go', 'declaration': 'Migrate'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['config-versioned-readers', 'config-durable-migration', 'config-durable-migration-os-entry'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': 'Migrate writes the Section 6.4 durable migration with an owner-only backup and atomic replacement, but no clause of Section 6.4 is enumerated against an acceptance case.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:6.5'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/config/validation.go', 'declaration': 'translateV3'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['config-versioned-readers', 'config-current-writer', 'config-durable-migration', 'config-durable-migration-os-entry'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': 'translateV3 maps the legacy terminal table into the Section 6.5 terminal configuration, but the Section 6.5 required_capabilities default is the platform lane minimum while internal/config/validation.go accepts only an empty default, and the sanitized ax doctor and terminal-backends inspection surface Section 6.5 requires does not exist; no clause of Section 6.5 is enumerated.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:17.1'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/meshneg/negotiate.go', 'declaration': 'Negotiate'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['meshneg-selection', 'rpcwire-version-boundary', 'config-versioned-readers'], 'coverage': 'partial', 'clauses': [{'id': '17.1#1', 'line': 15567, 'excerpt': '- a major increment MAY break syntax or semantics and MUST require explicit', 'acceptance_cases': ['meshneg-selection']}, {'id': '17.1#4', 'line': 15589, 'excerpt': 'highest mutually supported minor within a common major; they MUST NOT select a', 'acceptance_cases': ['meshneg-selection']}, {'id': '17.1#5', 'line': 15602, 'excerpt': 'immutable v0.1.0 contracts and MUST NOT be interpreted using the corrected', 'acceptance_cases': ['meshneg-selection', 'rpcwire-version-boundary']}], 'gap': 'Section 17.1 clauses 17.1#2 (minor-version semantic preservation) and 17.1#6 (v1 materialization upgrade) are outside Negotiate, which selects majors only: no minor-selection entry exists, immutable-object namespaced extensions (17.1#3) belong to the object-exchange owners, and materialization upgrade belongs to the matjournal and provhost owners. The retained config-versioned-readers case keeps the config Decode lanes traceable.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:17.2'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/cliresult/client.go', 'declaration': 'Read'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['cli-result-machine-reading', 'cli-result-identity-precedence', 'structured-error-identity-precedence', 'cli-result-historical-envelopes', 'structured-error-historical-envelopes', 'config-versioned-readers', 'config-current-writer', 'structured-error-common-data-model'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': "Section 17.2 carries exactly one scanner-visible obligation, clause 17.2#1: a reader MAY retain an unknown event as inert history but MUST NOT derive state from it. That clause binds Session Event history, and Read classifies one completed CLI invocation rather than retaining any event, so this binding discharges none of Section 17.2's measured obligations. The four numbered reader rules the section states carry no RFC 2119 keyword and are therefore invisible to the clause scanner; three of them are implemented and tested here - Read and Decode settle the schema and major before any other member, the closed member set included, acceptsVersion implements the same-or-lower-minor rule, and an unknown namespaced extension survives a decode and re-encode byte for byte - while the unknown ownership/security enum rule is covered only for the closed CLI Result vocabularies, not for any lease or security enum, Read classifies one completed CLI invocation, whose alphabet carries no lease or security enum, so the rule is discharged for the reader's own enums and silent for enums the reader never observes."}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:17.4'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/meshneg/negotiate.go', 'declaration': 'Negotiate'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['story-4qojoz-mesh-negotiation', 'config-read-only-downgrade', 'config-durable-migration'], 'coverage': 'sliver', 'clauses': [{'id': '17.4#4', 'line': 15661, 'excerpt': 'immutable evidence; it MUST report activation unavailable rather than omit the', 'acceptance_cases': ['story-4qojoz-mesh-negotiation']}], 'gap': 'Section 17.4 clauses 17.4#1 through 17.4#3 (upgrade checks, downgraded-binary read-only mode, no resume or transfer) are outside Negotiate: no upgrade, downgrade, or auto-resume flow exists in the tree, so only the activation-unavailable exposure clause discharges above. The retained config cases keep the AssessCompatibility downgrade-assessment lanes traceable.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:4.C'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/tmuxserver/lifecycle.go', 'declaration': 'Execute'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['tmux-attach-overlap-v070', 'tmux-attach-semantics-v070', 'tmux-lifecycle-operations-v070'], 'coverage': 'partial', 'gap': "Lifecycle.Execute discharges Section 4.C clauses 4.C#3, 4.C#4, 4.C#5, 4.C#6, and 4.C#7 for repeated identity, literal ax pane argv, host-only attach descriptors, AttachAuthorization equality, and listed refusal behavior. The creating uncertainty/status-first rule and per-side-effect winning-lease comparison remain outside this attach/lifecycle leaf's measured clauses.", 'clauses': [{'id': '4.C#3', 'line': 1155, 'excerpt': 'Every repeated identity MUST equal the request context.', 'acceptance_cases': ['tmux-attach-semantics-v070', 'tmux-lifecycle-operations-v070']}, {'id': '4.C#4', 'line': 1159, 'excerpt': '<code>{argv:string[3]}</code>, and its three values MUST be literal', 'acceptance_cases': ['tmux-lifecycle-operations-v070']}, {'id': '4.C#5', 'line': 1162, 'excerpt': '<code>string[1..4096]</code> usable only on the responding host and MUST NOT be', 'acceptance_cases': ['tmux-attach-semantics-v070']}, {'id': '4.C#6', 'line': 1189, 'excerpt': 'capability. In <code>attach</code>, the result input boolean MUST equal both the', 'acceptance_cases': ['tmux-attach-overlap-v070', 'tmux-attach-semantics-v070']}, {'id': '4.C#7', 'line': 1195, 'excerpt': 'An error not listed for an operation MUST NOT be emitted by the backend for a', 'acceptance_cases': ['tmux-attach-semantics-v070', 'tmux-lifecycle-operations-v070']}]}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:4.D'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/termbind/resolve.go', 'declaration': 'ResolveEvidence'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['terminal-evidence-resolution-exact'], 'coverage': 'sliver', 'gap': 'ResolveEvidence discharges Section 4.D clause 4.D#2 by admitting every resolved Manifest, Probe, and Capability Evidence object through the landed Registry.AdmitProbe, which verifies the attestation signature before the object is treated as evidence; forged signatures refuse. The other Section 4.D clauses (registry-row equality 4.D#1 and the no-silent-fallback backend selection rule 4.D#3) are landed Reconcile behavior and explicit-selection behavior respectively and stay unenumerated here.', 'clauses': [{'id': '4.D#2', 'line': 1296, 'excerpt': 'key registry and MUST verify the signature before treating the object as', 'acceptance_cases': ['terminal-evidence-resolution-exact']}]}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:5.1'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/canonicaljson/closed_shapes.go', 'declaration': 'validateSessionRecordWithDerivation'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['canonical-object-identity', 'canonical-identity-refusal'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': 'validateSessionRecordWithDerivation validates the Section 5.1 Session Record shape; the derivation and lifecycle behaviour Section 5.1 requires is not implemented, and the Launch Stdin member, the Curator extension keys and the fragment-digest rule Section 5.1 adds are not implemented, so no clause of Section 5.1 is enumerated. Pending implementation owner: STORY-260916-2q85nu.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:5.2'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/termbind/resolve.go', 'declaration': 'ResolveEvidence'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['catalog-v050-exact', 'core-record-identity-validation', 'terminal-evidence-resolution-exact', 'terminal-binding-events-exact'], 'coverage': 'sliver', 'gap': 'ResolveEvidence discharges Section 5.2 clauses 5.2#16 and 5.2#17 (evidence IDs resolve locally to validated Manifest/Probe/Evidence bound to the event tuple, never to a native reference or live-process fact); Section 5.2 clause 5.2#18 (v4 retained as inert immutable history, no derived state, no lower-version write) is pinned for Terminal Events by the EmitTerminalCreated emission path with sessrepo retention and the sessstate/sessquery readers (the retained-verbatim half, driven by TestV4RetainedAsImmutableHistory — the v1-only-reader half is a stated bound: no v1-v3-only reader exists on trunk). The other Section 5.2 envelope, table, authorship, ordering, and epoch clauses stay with the landed validateSessionEvent shape authority and sessrepo ordering, unenumerated here.', 'clauses': [{'id': '5.2#16', 'line': 1971, 'excerpt': 'replicated. The evidence IDs MUST resolve locally to validated, sanitized', 'acceptance_cases': ['terminal-evidence-resolution-exact']}, {'id': '5.2#17', 'line': 1973, 'excerpt': 'backend ID and versions. They MUST NOT resolve through the event to a native', 'acceptance_cases': ['terminal-evidence-resolution-exact']}, {'id': '5.2#18', 'line': 1984, 'excerpt': 'as inert immutable history but MUST NOT derive runtime state or write a lower-', 'acceptance_cases': ['terminal-binding-events-exact']}]}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:5.3'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/sessrepo/lease_store.go', 'declaration': 'CompareAndSwapLease'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['lease-record-lifecycle', 'lease-fencing-revalidation', 'lease-checkpoint-admission', 'lease-divergent-preservation', 'lease-union-resolution', 'lease-fencing-gates', 'core-record-identity-validation', 'lease-ownership-union-properties', 'lease-ownership-store-properties', 'story-260917-append-winning-lease-admission'], 'coverage': 'partial', 'gap': "CompareAndSwapLease with the fencing gates discharges 7 of the 8 Section 5.3 clauses; clause 5.3#5 (every new takeover lease MUST use max_observed_epoch + 1 from the initiator's union) stays unimplemented because the union maximum is caller-side input and no takeover flow exists in this repository yet. The ownership property cases (union-order independence and loser preservation over Reduce, clock non-authority and single authority over the lease store) add executable proofs for the discharged 5.3#6 and 5.3#7 divergent-preservation evidence without changing the 7-of-8 ratio.", 'clauses': [{'id': '5.3#1', 'line': 2006, 'excerpt': '| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | MUST equal <code>issued_by_host_id</code> |', 'acceptance_cases': ['core-record-identity-validation']}, {'id': '5.3#2', 'line': 2036, 'excerpt': 'tie-break. A valid epoch greater than 1 MUST name a known predecessor for the', 'acceptance_cases': ['lease-record-lifecycle', 'lease-checkpoint-admission']}, {'id': '5.3#3', 'line': 2037, 'excerpt': "same session, MUST equal that predecessor's epoch plus one, and MUST reference", 'acceptance_cases': ['lease-record-lifecycle', 'lease-checkpoint-admission']}, {'id': '5.3#4', 'line': 2039, 'excerpt': '<code>create</code> lease MUST have a null predecessor and MAY have a null', 'acceptance_cases': ['lease-record-lifecycle']}, {'id': '5.3#6', 'line': 2046, 'excerpt': 'lease wins. Events under the losing same-epoch lease and all lower epochs MUST', 'acceptance_cases': ['lease-divergent-preservation', 'lease-union-resolution', 'lease-ownership-union-properties', 'story-260917-append-winning-lease-admission']}, {'id': '5.3#7', 'line': 2047, 'excerpt': 'be preserved in a divergent branch and MUST NOT affect authoritative state.', 'acceptance_cases': ['lease-divergent-preservation', 'lease-union-resolution', 'lease-ownership-union-properties', 'story-260917-append-winning-lease-admission']}, {'id': '5.3#8', 'line': 2049, 'excerpt': 'An owner process MUST revalidate its fencing token before:', 'acceptance_cases': ['lease-fencing-revalidation', 'lease-fencing-gates']}]}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:5.4'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/sessckpt/capture.go', 'declaration': 'Capture'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['workspace-checkpoint-capture', 'workspace-checkpoint-admission'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': 'Capture durably installs Section 5.4 checkpoint records with attested identities, idempotent replays, and head-bound admission; restore behaviour is not implemented and no clause of Section 5.4 is enumerated.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:5.5'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/provhost/identity_create.go', 'declaration': 'CreateIdentity'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['provhost-identity-create', 'provhost-identity-check'], 'coverage': 'sliver', 'gap': "Section 5.5 clause 5.5#1 stays undisclosed: its opaque-map MUST NOT names credentials, environment values, PIDs, sockets, terminal IDs, and mutable cache selectors, and CreateIdentity decides only the absolute-path half, because no string-value test can decide the rest. Clause 5.5#2's destination-derivation MUST belongs to the destination adapter rather than the host record.", 'clauses': [{'id': '5.5#3', 'line': 2203, 'excerpt': '<code>backend_conversation_uuid</code> with null realm fingerprint. Each MUST fail schema or provider-identity validation.', 'acceptance_cases': ['provhost-identity-create', 'provhost-identity-check']}]}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:5.6'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/canonicaljson/core_records.go', 'declaration': 'validateWorkspaceGroupRecord'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['core-record-identity-validation'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': 'validateWorkspaceGroupRecord validates the Section 5.6 workspace group shape; workspace group membership and union behaviour is not implemented and no clause of Section 5.6 is enumerated.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:7.2'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/catalog/catalog.go', 'declaration': 'ForRelease'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['catalog-v050-exact'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': 'ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 7.2; the Section 7.2 host envelope (framing, deadlines, size limits, dispatch, and recovery) is implemented in internal/provhost under the Section 7.6 and Section 7.7 bindings, and no clause of Section 7.2 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 7 obligations it carries.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:7.3'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/catalog/catalog.go', 'declaration': 'ForRelease'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['catalog-v050-exact'], 'coverage': 'unmeasured', 'gap': 'ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 7.3; the RFC 2119 scanner measures no clause line under 7.3, because the closed Provider Manifest states its obligations as a required-member table, a 16-entry operation registry and a nine-name capability registry (seven names under 1.0.0) rather than in uppercase keywords, so the gate cannot measure this section - and the 1.1.0 caller_launch_plan and stdin_resume_replay names are unimplemented. Pending implementation owner: STORY-260916-1ea7od; the seven-name 1.0.0 manifest stays implemented in internal/provhost DecodeManifest, exercised by the provhost conformance suite.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:3.2'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/tmuxserver/bind.go', 'declaration': 'CheckSocketCustody'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['AC-PATH-001', 'localstore-path-registry', 'localstore-layout-owner-only', 'localstore-digest-path-v1', 'localstore-immutable-blob-install', 'localstore-sqlite-projection', 'tmux-socket-custody-v070'], 'coverage': 'sliver', 'gap': "CheckSocketCustody discharges Section 3.2 clause 3.2#8 for the socket's kind, owner, private mode, and identity recheck before Probe connects, Lifecycle dispatches, or Spawner unlinks. ResolvePaths and the listed localstore cases remain the path/layout owners; the other Section 3.2 clauses stay unenumerated here.", 'clauses': [{'id': '3.2#8', 'line': 810, 'excerpt': 'symlink. Before bind, connect, rename, or unlink, AX MUST reject a socket path,', 'acceptance_cases': ['tmux-socket-custody-v070']}]}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:3.3'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/localstore/projection.go', 'declaration': 'OpenProjection'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['localstore-sqlite-projection'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': 'OpenProjection rebuilds and recovers the Section 3.3 SQLite projection, but the replication-exclusion clause and the wire-compatibility-signal clause have no implementation and no clause of Section 3.3 is enumerated.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:7.4'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/catalog/catalog.go', 'declaration': 'ForRelease'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['catalog-v050-exact'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': 'ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 7.4; the 1.1.0 probe response with nine capability keys is unimplemented, and no clause of 7.4 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 1 obligation it carries. Pending implementation owner: STORY-260916-1ea7od.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:7.5'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/catalog/catalog.go', 'declaration': 'ForRelease'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['catalog-v050-exact'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': 'ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 7.5; the host-side Section 7.5 operation conformance (SpawnPlan launch and resume bodies, identify-session results, materialize-status recovery, and the single operation plus operation_id mutation key) is implemented in internal/provhost under the Section 7.6 and Section 7.7 bindings, the SpawnPlan.stdin member, the resume.launch_plan member and the stdin replay rule are unimplemented, and no clause of Section 7.5 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 56 obligations it carries. Pending implementation owner: STORY-260916-1kp1lx.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:7.A'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/terminalbackend/descriptor.go', 'declaration': 'AdmitProviderDescriptor'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['terminal-provider-descriptor-7a', 'terminal-instance-identity-exact'], 'coverage': 'partial', 'gap': 'AdmitProviderDescriptor discharges Section 7.A clause 7.A#1 (the Provider rejects a descriptor whose binding digest, backend, version, or generation does not match the AX-validated binding), pinned by the landed terminal-provider-descriptor-7a mismatch tests and the terminal-instance-identity-exact eight-form identity pin through the same entry. Section 7.A clause 7.A#2 (LeaseToken v2 fencing rules and the 3.x transport envelope) stays with provhost v2 machinery and the dual-stack follow-up, undisclosed here.', 'clauses': [{'id': '7.A#1', 'line': 3724, 'excerpt': 'TerminalBackend. The Provider MUST reject a descriptor whose binding digest,', 'acceptance_cases': ['terminal-provider-descriptor-7a', 'terminal-instance-identity-exact']}]}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:7.1'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/provider/provider.go', 'declaration': 'Discover'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['provider-discovery-and-trust'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': 'Discover implements the Section 7.1 deterministic discovery, trust recording, and substitution detection with the section-mandated duplicate invalid_config refusal; no clause of Section 7.1 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 6 obligations it carries.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:7.6'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/provhost/quiesce.go', 'declaration': 'DecodeQuiesceProof'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['provhost-quiesce-proof'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': 'DecodeQuiesceProof implements the Section 7.6 quiescence proof decoder with its fail-closed safe-bit rules; the Provider Identity Record it carries is additionally checked by CheckIdentity, and no clause of Section 7.6 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 3 obligations it carries.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:7.7'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/provhost/profile_resolve.go', 'declaration': 'ResolveMapping'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['provhost-mapping-resolution', 'provhost-profile-mapping', 'provhost-launch-projection'], 'coverage': 'partial', 'gap': 'Section 7.7 clause 7.7#2 stays undisclosed: its omit rule is enforced, but its machine-local-alias sentence is only half-decided, because a shell word that expands to unrestricted mode without spelling a table token is beyond argv inspection (shell aliases never expand under execve, owned by secprim). ResolveMapping decides the exact-version probe rule the other three clauses need.', 'clauses': [{'id': '7.7#1', 'line': 3689, 'excerpt': "<code>standard</code> MUST use the provider's normal approval/sandbox behavior", 'acceptance_cases': ['provhost-profile-mapping', 'provhost-launch-projection']}, {'id': '7.7#3', 'line': 3697, 'excerpt': 'MUST disclose that equivalence;', 'acceptance_cases': ['provhost-mapping-resolution']}, {'id': '7.7#4', 'line': 3700, 'excerpt': 'The adapter MUST probe the exact provider version before applying a mapping.', 'acceptance_cases': ['provhost-mapping-resolution']}]}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:8'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/resumesmoke/smoke.go', 'declaration': 'Run'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['provhost-resume-tuple-gate', 'resumesmoke-matrix', 'resumesmoke-run', 'resumesmoke-record', 'resumesmoke-store'], 'coverage': 'sliver', 'gap': 'Section 8 clauses 8#4 through 8#9 (the per-provider materialization rules), 8#10 (the capability-plane split), and 8#11 (ConPTY acceptance) stay undisclosed: Run enforces the native-resume direction and refuses unsupported tuples but stages no store, merges no bytes, and proves no terminal. No provider materialization exists anywhere in this repository.', 'clauses': [{'id': '8#1', 'line': 4102, 'excerpt': 'probe still MUST succeed;', 'acceptance_cases': ['resumesmoke-run']}, {'id': '8#2', 'line': 4109, 'excerpt': 'unknown MUST NOT be rewritten as unsupported,', 'acceptance_cases': ['resumesmoke-matrix', 'resumesmoke-run']}, {'id': '8#3', 'line': 4110, 'excerpt': 'conditional MUST NOT be advertised as available.', 'acceptance_cases': ['resumesmoke-matrix', 'resumesmoke-run']}, {'id': '8#12', 'line': 4183, 'excerpt': 'The release MUST NOT collapse WSL2 and native Windows into one row.', 'acceptance_cases': ['provhost-resume-tuple-gate', 'resumesmoke-matrix']}]}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:7.8'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/sessadapter/protocol.go', 'declaration': 'DecodeRequestFrame'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['session-adapter-frame-bound', 'session-adapter-call-binding'], 'coverage': 'full', 'clauses': [{'id': '7.8#1', 'line': 3785, 'excerpt': 'Large data is referenced by manifest or Blob Descriptor ID and MUST NOT be embedded in the 8 MiB frame.', 'acceptance_cases': ['session-adapter-frame-bound']}, {'id': '7.8#2', 'line': 3912, 'excerpt': 'target mutation, these facts MUST equal freshly read trusted-candidate facts and the Journal binding.', 'acceptance_cases': ['session-adapter-call-binding']}]}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:7.9'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/catalog/catalog.go', 'declaration': 'ForRelease'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['catalog-v050-exact'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': 'ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 7.9; no clause of 7.9 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 8 obligations it carries.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:9.2'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/catalog/catalog.go', 'declaration': 'ForRelease'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['catalog-v050-exact'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': 'ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 9.2; no clause of 9.2 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 35 obligations it carries.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:10.8.5'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/catalog/catalog.go', 'declaration': 'ForRelease'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['catalog-v050-exact'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': 'ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 10.8.5; no clause of 10.8.5 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 4 obligations it carries.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:10.1'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/canonicaljson/closed_shapes.go', 'declaration': 'validateImmutableObjectShape'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['scalar-digest-validation', 'scalar-timestamp-validation', 'scalar-uuid-validation', 'canonical-object-identity', 'canonical-identity-refusal', 'core-record-identity-validation', 'localstore-immutable-blob-install'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': 'validateImmutableObjectShape enforces the Section 10.1 common envelope, but the digest-derived storage path clause and the quarantine-and-stop clause are implemented in internal/localstore rather than by this binding, and no clause of Section 10.1 is enumerated.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:10.2'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/clonesnap/capture.go', 'declaration': 'Capture'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['scalar-digest-validation', 'scalar-bounded-integer-validation', 'canonical-jcs-rfc8785', 'canonical-object-identity', 'canonical-identity-refusal', 'localstore-digest-path-v1', 'localstore-immutable-blob-install', 'localstore-sqlite-projection', 'clone-capture-contracts', 'clone-native-capture', 'clone-projection-fidelity'], 'coverage': 'full', 'clauses': [{'id': '10.2#1', 'line': 4854, 'excerpt': 'MUST live in a manifest, not in the blob path.', 'acceptance_cases': ['clone-capture-contracts']}, {'id': '10.2#2', 'line': 4855, 'excerpt': 'references a blob, the writer MUST fsync the blob, verify its size and digest, and atomically install it in the object store.', 'acceptance_cases': ['clone-native-capture', 'clone-projection-fidelity', 'localstore-immutable-blob-install']}, {'id': '10.2#3', 'line': 4859, 'excerpt': 'metrics MUST record digest, size, and media type only, never blob contents.', 'acceptance_cases': ['clone-native-capture']}, {'id': '10.2#4', 'line': 4862, 'excerpt': '<code>urn:ax:schema:blob</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Chunks MUST be sorted, contiguous, non-overlapping, start at offset zero, and cover exactly <code>size</code> bytes:', 'acceptance_cases': ['clone-native-capture']}, {'id': '10.2#5', 'line': 4902, 'excerpt': 'A larger file MUST fail capture with <code>capability_unavailable</code> before publishing a partial manifest.', 'acceptance_cases': ['clone-native-capture']}]}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:10.3'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/canonicaljson/closed_shapes.go', 'declaration': 'validateBlobDescriptor'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['scalar-bounded-integer-validation', 'scalar-digest-validation', 'canonical-identity-refusal'], 'coverage': 'sliver', 'gap': 'validateBlobDescriptor enforces the Section 10.3 chunk offset invariant, but the two receiver clauses - validate every chunk before marking it present, and validate the complete blob after assembly - have no implementation because no transfer receiver exists.', 'clauses': [{'id': '10.3#1', 'line': 4914, 'excerpt': '<code>chunk_id:digest</code>. It has no extension map. Offset MUST equal index times 4,194,304; every non-final chunk has that exact size.', 'acceptance_cases': ['canonical-identity-refusal']}]}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:10.4'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/canonicaljson/closed_shapes.go', 'declaration': 'validateTransferManifest'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['scalar-closed-enum-validation', 'scalar-uuid-validation', 'scalar-digest-validation', 'canonical-object-identity', 'canonical-identity-refusal'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': 'validateTransferManifest validates the Section 10.4 Transfer Manifest shape; the transfer, staging and conflict behaviour Section 10.4 requires is not implemented and no clause of Section 10.4 is enumerated.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:10.6'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/matjournal/store.go', 'declaration': 'Create'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['materialization-journal-lifecycle'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': 'Create durably installs Section 10.6 materialization journals with phase transitions, receipts, and input digests; provider, bridge, and replica effects stay modeled and no clause of Section 10.6 is enumerated.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:11.2'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/rpcwire/envelope.go', 'declaration': 'DecodeRequest'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['rpcwire-closed-bodies', 'rpcwire-framing', 'catalog-v050-exact'], 'coverage': 'partial', 'clauses': [{'id': '11.2#2', 'line': 7364, 'excerpt': 'state, Structured Error, Observation Event, and CLI Result MUST NOT appear in', 'acceptance_cases': ['rpcwire-closed-bodies']}, {'id': '11.2#3', 'line': 7408, 'excerpt': '<code>ok = false</code> and one Structured Error and MUST omit body. Unknown', 'acceptance_cases': ['rpcwire-framing']}, {'id': '11.2#4', 'line': 7420, 'excerpt': 'at least the values shown and MUST refuse a peer below them. The 5 MiB object', 'acceptance_cases': ['rpcwire-closed-bodies']}], 'gap': 'Section 11.2 clauses 11.2#1 and 11.2#5 (hello-first sequencing) are executed only for the RPC-5 Host Channel responder: DecodeRequest is a stateless codec with no handshake memory, and no legacy `ax rpc serve` responder exists in the tree, so the legacy sequencing lane stays a stated bound while the codec-enforced clauses discharge above.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:11.3'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/catalog/catalog.go', 'declaration': 'ForRelease'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['catalog-v050-exact'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': 'ForRelease returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 11.3. rpcwire now validates inventory.roots namespace/cardinality (6/7/8/8 across RPC 2/3/4/5) and matches roots to requested namespaces, and hostchannel dispatches authorized post-hello inventory.roots calls through the current-generation gate (TestInventoryRootsThroughChannel). No Merkle digest verification, schema membership or object exchange exists. No clause of 11.3 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 27 obligations it carries.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:11.8'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/catalog/catalog.go', 'declaration': 'ForRelease'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['catalog-v050-exact'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': 'ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 11.8. rpcwire pins the exact historical 24-key RPC-3 hello map and 7-namespace inventory syntax (contracts-v3 fixture); no negotiation, object exchange or clause of 11.8 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 4 obligations it carries.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:11.9'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/catalog/catalog.go', 'declaration': 'ForRelease'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['catalog-v050-exact'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': 'ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 11.9. rpcwire pins the exact 25-key RPC-4 hello map and 8-namespace inventory syntax (contracts-v4 fixture) and reuses those shapes for RPC 5 with contracts.rpc [5.0.0]; no TerminalBackend evidence replication or clause of 11.9 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 2 obligations it carries.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:13.12'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/matjournal/recover.go', 'declaration': 'Recover'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['materialization-journal-recovery', 'crash-gate-journal-conformance'], 'coverage': 'unmeasured', 'gap': 'Recover classifies the journal-observable Section 13.12 failure rows (operator interrupt, owner-resume response lost, atomic rename blocked, disk full, task-board import/open/adopt failure before and after the new lease) into the Section 13.13 outcomes, proved by the crashgate conformance harness; the scanner finds no clause line in the table-shaped Section 13.12 so the binding stays unmeasured, and rows owned by sync, lease, provider, bridge, and lifecycle flows (SSH disconnect, quarantine, divergence, quiesce failure, plugin crash, missing bridge, concurrent takeovers, stale owner, corrupt index) belong to their unlanded owners.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:13.13'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/matjournal/recover.go', 'declaration': 'Recover'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['materialization-journal-recovery', 'crash-gate-journal-conformance', 'crash-gate-checkpoint-conformance'], 'coverage': 'partial', 'gap': 'Recover with the crashgate conformance harness discharges 9 of the 11 normative clauses of Section 13.13 (every-boundary injection for checkpoint/journal-observable paths, exactly-one classification, safe_retry meaning, ambiguity rule, no fourth outcome, conformance record contents, two-live-authority and substitution rejection, unfenced-continuation parking); clauses 13.13#4 and 13.13#5 are discharged only for their journal-durable halves because rollback/parked visibility through event, CLI/status, audit, and lifecycle-projection surfaces belongs to unlanded owners, and boundaries owned by lease, terminal, provider, bridge, sync, lifecycle, and clone flows are recorded NOT APPLICABLE with owners rather than injected.', 'clauses': [{'id': '13.13#1', 'line': 10250, 'excerpt': 'Every implementation MUST inject a crash and a clean process restart at every', 'acceptance_cases': ['crash-gate-journal-conformance', 'crash-gate-checkpoint-conformance']}, {'id': '13.13#2', 'line': 10252, 'excerpt': 'After restart, the recovery evaluator MUST classify the operation into exactly', 'acceptance_cases': ['crash-gate-journal-conformance']}, {'id': '13.13#3', 'line': 10257, 'excerpt': '| <code>safe_retry</code> | The same logical operation can continue or return its recorded result using every caller-stable operation/materialization/transaction/bridge ID and byte-identical immutable input. The winning lease and the exact persisted Provider Identity Record or task-board manager reference/Ax Binding are unchanged. A retry MUST reconcile an uncertain external effect before issuing it again and MUST NOT allocate another process, manager, native handle, lease epoch, staging authority, or transaction root. | The pre-crash durable receipt or journal phase, the post-restart status result for every possibly executed provider/bridge/external effect, the unchanged winning lease, the unchanged native identity/binding, and the single returned or advanced durable result. |', 'acceptance_cases': ['crash-gate-journal-conformance', 'crash-gate-checkpoint-conformance']}, {'id': '13.13#6', 'line': 10268, 'excerpt': 'contradictory, unreachable, or ambiguous evidence MUST select', 'acceptance_cases': ['crash-gate-journal-conformance']}, {'id': '13.13#7', 'line': 10269, 'excerpt': '<code>recoverable_parked_state</code>; an implementation MUST NOT invent a', 'acceptance_cases': ['crash-gate-journal-conformance']}, {'id': '13.13#8', 'line': 10277, 'excerpt': 'phases still is. The conformance record MUST name the boundary ID, path,', 'acceptance_cases': ['crash-gate-journal-conformance', 'crash-gate-checkpoint-conformance']}, {'id': '13.13#9', 'line': 10297, 'excerpt': 'For every boundary, the gate MUST reject the run if two hosts or two native', 'acceptance_cases': ['crash-gate-journal-conformance']}, {'id': '13.13#10', 'line': 10301, 'excerpt': 'MUST be fenced/stopped with visible divergent-history evidence or remain', 'acceptance_cases': ['crash-gate-journal-conformance']}, {'id': '13.13#11', 'line': 10302, 'excerpt': '<code>recoverable_parked_state</code>. The gate also MUST reject any recovery', 'acceptance_cases': ['crash-gate-journal-conformance']}]}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:13.14.5'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/canonicaljson/core_records.go', 'declaration': 'validateSessionEventV2'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['catalog-v050-exact', 'core-record-identity-validation'], 'coverage': 'unmeasured', 'gap': 'validateSessionEventV2 validates the Section 13.14.5 v2 Session Event shape, which is topically the subject of the section; the RFC 2119 scanner measures no clause line under 13.14.5, because the section states its obligations as required-member and variant tables rather than in uppercase keywords, so the gate cannot measure how much of the section this binding actually discharges.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:13.15'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/canonicaljson/core_records.go', 'declaration': 'validateSessionEventV3'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['catalog-v050-exact', 'core-record-identity-validation'], 'coverage': 'unevidenced', 'gap': 'validateSessionEventV3 validates the Section 13.15 event payload shape, but no clause of Section 13.15 is enumerated against an acceptance case.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:15.1'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/axerror/axerror.go', 'declaration': 'New'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['structured-error-exact-object', 'structured-error-shape-refusal', 'structured-error-detail-redaction', 'structured-error-detail-inertness', 'structured-error-static-binding', 'structured-error-unknown-code-reader', 'structured-error-local-untrusted', 'cli-result-message-independence', 'structured-error-historical-envelopes', 'structured-error-identity-precedence', 'structured-error-common-data-model'], 'coverage': 'partial', 'gap': 'Two of the seven Section 15.1 clauses stay unimplemented here. Clause 15.1#5 is the RPC hello obligation - an error contract key must never be advertised or negotiated in a hello frame - and New builds a failure object rather than a hello frame; rpcwire now builds and rejects structural hello frames through its public codec and hostchannel consumes them in the authenticated handshake (Serve/Dial), while BindingFor stays a static table with no negotiation path; the clause itself is still not enumerated against an acceptance case. Clause 15.1#6 is the Provider JSON-over-stdio bootstrap row, whose only RFC 2119 sentence is that the plugin MUST NOT masquerade a different-major object as v2; that obligation binds the provider plugin and this repository builds no provider plugin, only the cataloggen and tracecheck binaries. LocalFromUntrusted implements the host half of the same row, but that half states no RFC 2119 keyword, so it discharges nothing the clause scanner measures and is claimed for clause 15.1#7 instead.', 'clauses': [{'id': '15.1#1', 'line': 15133, 'excerpt': 'MUST be present when known. Messages are for humans; automation MUST branch on', 'acceptance_cases': ['structured-error-exact-object', 'structured-error-detail-inertness', 'cli-result-message-independence', 'structured-error-historical-envelopes']}, {'id': '15.1#2', 'line': 15134, 'excerpt': '<code>code</code> and <code>exit_code</code>. Details MUST be redacted and', 'acceptance_cases': ['structured-error-detail-redaction']}, {'id': '15.1#3', 'line': 15141, 'excerpt': 'maximum canonical size 16 KiB. Readers MAY ignore unknown detail keys and MUST', 'acceptance_cases': ['structured-error-shape-refusal', 'structured-error-detail-inertness']}, {'id': '15.1#4', 'line': 15150, 'excerpt': 'supported-major failure MUST use that exact object; the containing protocol', 'acceptance_cases': ['structured-error-static-binding', 'structured-error-historical-envelopes']}, {'id': '15.1#7', 'line': 15184, 'excerpt': 'IDs and records redacted diagnostics only. Receivers MUST NOT parse a different', 'acceptance_cases': ['structured-error-local-untrusted', 'structured-error-unknown-code-reader']}]}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:15.2'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/axerror/registry.go', 'declaration': 'ExitCodeFor'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['structured-error-code-exit-registry', 'cli-result-exit-status-mapping', 'structured-error-exit-status-fan-in'], 'coverage': 'unmeasured', 'gap': 'Section 15.2 states its eighteen-row exit-code registry as a table with no RFC 2119 keyword, so the clause scanner measures zero obligations and ExitCodeFor cannot discharge a clause this gate can see. The table is implemented and checked row for row against the pinned text - TestExitStatusRegistryMatchesThePinnedTableRowForRow measures the row count and every status from internal/specdoc rather than restating them - and internal/cliresult now maps a failure to that exact process status through Emit and ExitStatus. What is still missing is the process itself: this repository builds no ax binary, and the only os.Exit calls in the tree are the exit(1) failure paths of cataloggen and tracecheck, so nothing here ever terminates with a Section 15.2 status.'}, {'kind': 'section_binding', 'keys': ['section:15.3'], 'production': {'path': 'internal/axerror/registry.go', 'declaration': 'ExitCodeFor'}, 'acceptance_cases': ['structured-error-code-exit-registry', 'structured-error-unknown-code-reader', 'structured-error-typed-details', 'cli-result-historical-envelopes', 'structured-error-exit-status-fan-in'], 'coverage': 'partial', 'gap': 'Clause 15.3#3 additionally forbids Structured Error from appearing as an RPC hello key or a TerminalBackend capability, and ExitCodeFor resolves a code-to-exit mapping rather than building either advertisement. rpcwire builds structural hello frames and rejects an error map key (TestHelloRefusals/error-key), hostchannel frames failures only as Error envelopes and never as hello keys, and the closed 16-capability admission registry in internal/terminalbackend is never advertised on an RPC hell