/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/planning-workflow.md-213-- **The coordinator is a SUPERVISOR — it does NOT write code itself**
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/planning-workflow.md-214-- ALL implementation work (code, tests, docs updates) goes to sub-agents
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/planning-workflow.md-215-- **Choose the strongest suitable registered model deliberately for every child** — maximize quality per token: use stronger capability for genuinely complex analysis, architecture, implementation, or review; choose balanced, fast, or cost-sensitive registered options only when they can pass the same required quality gates. Never rely on model or reasoning inheritance.
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/planning-workflow.md:216:- **Prepare tasks before spawning:** ensure each task has clear README (title, description, scope, AC) and link any instructions/specs as precondition resources via `task-board m 'add_resource(..., type=precondition)'`, with task-scoped resource names
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/planning-workflow.md-217-- **Spawn explicitly:** `task-board spawn TASK-260218-abc --role developer --background --agent codex --model gpt-5.6-sol --reasoning-effort max` auto-composes prompt from task README + resources + role identity
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/planning-workflow.md-218-- **Agent naming:** automatic with roles for Claude, Codex, and Qwen children. Archetype is visible in the dashboard.
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/planning-workflow.md-219-- Spawn sub-agents in parallel for independent stories (same phase)
