/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/resources-and-bugs.md-97-## Best Practices
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/resources-and-bugs.md-98-
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/resources-and-bugs.md-99-- **Use preconditions for agent instructions** — attach design docs, specs, or step-by-step instructions before spawning
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/resources-and-bugs.md-100-- **Use outcomes for work products** — research findings, analysis, implementation notes
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/resources-and-bugs.md-101-- **Attach to the owning element** — pass the Task, Bug, Story, or Epic ID that owns the artifact; the storage layer groups its payloads under that element directory automatically
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/resources-and-bugs.md:102:- **Use explicit create/update/delete** — `add_resource` / `resource add` must not silently overwrite; use `update_resource` / `resource update` when replacing an existing payload
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/resources-and-bugs.md-103-- **Use adopt only for local repair** — `resource adopt` registers bytes already stored at `.resources/<elementID>/<relative-resource-path>` without rewriting them; a missing payload returns resource-not-found and an existing declaration returns resource-exists
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/resources-and-bugs.md-104-- **Choose a useful hierarchy inside the owning element** — `findings/`, `artifacts/`, `reports/`, and `revisions/` are conventions, not a fixed schema; nest further when it makes the handoff easier to navigate
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/resources-and-bugs.md:105:- **Use safe relative resource paths** — `/` separates validated path segments; empty, dot/traversal, absolute/drive-qualified, backslash, control-character, malformed escape, and encoded/repeatedly encoded separator or traversal forms are rejected in local and remote storage
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/resources-and-bugs.md-106-- **Attach files, not folders** — directories only organize resource files and never satisfy resource existence or handoff evidence
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/resources-and-bugs.md-107-- **Always use board commands** — never create/edit resource files or progress.md resource sections manually
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/resources-and-bugs.md-108-- **Name handoff evidence with task scope** — keep the task ID in the resource path, for example `reports/TASK-260218-abc_architecture-design.md`, so `task-board handoff` can recognize it
