/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/statuses.md:284:**Board-state close rule.** A Story ends with its board-state commit on trunk, delta or not. A Story that `integrate` or `complete` closed already has one (`Record <STORY-ID> board state`). Every other close — hand `set_status(done)`, research with no repository delta, a candidate that landed outside the control root, `close-landed`, `integrate_external` — owes `task-board board commit <STORY-ID>` as the next step, run by the orchestrator or operator from the control root on trunk. `task-board validate` reports `board_state_uncommitted` while a done element's lane paths are dirty; the commit, not the acknowledgement, clears it — `commit_ack=scope_committed` asserts the repository scope is on trunk and explicitly excludes the Story's own board delta.
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/statuses.md-285-
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/statuses.md-286-`board commit` follows the same commit-time rule as `integrate`: with `version_control.confirm` on, `--commit-time` RFC3339 is required and sets both dates; otherwise the current time is used. A stated commit time is never a publication time.
