/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/file-formats.md:622:`task-board validate` reports three distinct categories: `PROJECTION_CYCLE_DETECTED` is an advisory warning for story/epic cycles derived from task links or involving explicit legacy container links; `TASK_CYCLE_DETECTED` is an error for task/bug cycles; `UNSUPPORTED_CONTAINER_LINK` is a separate warning for stored container links without task-level support. A task DAG can have a container projection cycle without being invalid. `task-board repair-links` lists the same suspicious edges without writing. With `--confirm`, it selects and revalidates the requested edges inside one serialized board mutation, then removes only those that are still unsupported immediately before the write. It does not remove read-time derived edges or task-cycle links. See [plan dependency diagnostics](querying.md#plan-dependency-diagnostics) for `projection_cycles` and the `CycleNodes` compatibility note.
