-# TASK-260830-g0pcnt Results
-
-## Handoff state
-
-The tmux attach implementation and its task-level evidence are ready for review. The task is not handed off yet: the final Story registry requirement is blocked by trunk moving after this Story workspace was pinned. The exact synchronization blocker and required operator action are recorded in UNRESOLVED_QUESTIONS.md and below.
-
-The candidate is uncommitted on Story checkpoint cf2ad952176d470caad454c0c161ae8253260d54, as required. No Git branch operation or control-root file edit was performed.
-
-## Acceptance coverage
-
-**4 of 4 task acceptance rows are driven through production entries by named tests.**
-
-| AC row | Production entry | Named test evidence | Result |
-|---|---|---|---|
-| Lost-response idempotency | Lifecycle.Execute → executeAttach | TestExecuteAttachLostResponseReplaysRecordedOutcome | Same request key returns the recorded vector, receipt, effect evidence, and original timestamp; no second staging/install, receipt write, or retry exec. N-attach-lost-response-replay kills the replay bypass. |
-| Reconnect and multi-attach policy | Lifecycle.Execute(attach) → executeAttach/checkAttachOverlap | TestAttachSameClientRetryWithPeerPresent; TestAttachOverlapRequiresMultiAttach; TestAttachOverlapRequiresMultipleInputClients; TestAttachOverlapAdmissionAtomicAcrossLifecycleInstances | A verified same-client retry is replayed with a peer present. A new overlapping client requires multi_attach; concurrent input additionally requires multiple_input_clients and AX policy. The durable peer census and cross-Lifecycle lock remain the vcx6yo authority. Isolated overlap narrowings are listed in the conformance matrix. |
-| Socket substitution refusal | ServerProber.Probe; ServerSpawner.Spawn; all eight Lifecycle.Execute operation dispatches | TestServerProberRefusesSocketSubstitutionBeforeConnect; TestServerSpawnerRefusesSocketSubstitutionBeforeUnlinkOrSpawn; TestExecuteEveryOperationRefusesSocketSubstitutionBeforeDispatch | Changed inode, symlink, foreign owner, and permissive mode refuse before Dial, unlink/spawn, or lifecycle dispatch. The final-lstat-to-connect interval remains bound B46. |
-| Ownership-neutral attach | Lifecycle.Execute(attach) → executeAttach | TestExecuteAttachDoesNotReadOrChangeSessionLease | Attach neither reads nor refreshes the lease; durable lease and session event chain are unchanged. N-attach-ownership-neutral kills a lease-refresh narrowing. |
-
-### Inherited handoffs also closed
-
-- Read-only to writable escalation: TestExecuteAttachReadOnlyReceiptCannotEscalateToWritable drives Lifecycle.Execute. It asserts literal idempotency_mismatch, no vector, and no receipt mutation. N-attach-readonly-to-writable weakens the landed store refusal and the behavior test fails.
-- Foreground composition: TestForegroundAcquireComposesProductionProbeWithAttach drives the real Production probe through foreground Acquire and Lifecycle.Execute(attach) with a private live Unix socket. No tmux process starts.
-- Fresh-decoy foreground wiring: TestAcquireForegroundRefusesEveryCatalogDecoyRunning drives foreground Acquire. N-foreground-fresh-decoy-wiring admits only a fresh headless_creation decoy and is killed by the production-entry test.
-
-No new capability is advertised. The tests use a real Unix socket fixture but do not launch tmux. B44 remains an explicit liveness bound owned by a future authoritative receipt/protocol owner: an attach receipt is not positive evidence that the client remains connected.
-
-## Negative and narrowing evidence
-
-Twelve isolated narrowing mutants were killed; the harmless comment-only control survived. Raw logs and effect assertions are in the evidence archive.
-
-- Socket custody: N-socket-identity-swap, N-socket-symlink, N-socket-ownership, and N-socket-permissions. The permission mutant preserves the CheckSocketCustody source token while admitting exactly a 0644 socket; behavioral caller-entry tests fail before connect, dispatch, unlink, or spawn.
-- Attach replay and ownership: N-attach-lost-response-replay, N-attach-readonly-to-writable, and N-attach-ownership-neutral.
-- Overlap/generation: N-attach-overlap-multi, N-attach-overlap-input, N-attach-overlap-replay-unproven, and N-attach-postlock-generation.
-- Foreground wiring: N-foreground-fresh-decoy-wiring.
-- Control: C-control survived.
-
-The complete gate × production-entry census and six-axis tables are reproduced in TASK-260830-g0pcnt_conformance-matrix.md and mirrored in internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md. This leaf directly measures 6 of 30 gate-axis cells; the other 24 are explicitly bounded or unreachable with an owner/reason. The inherited attach-overlap census measures 16 of 36 cells and names 20 bounds/unreachable cells.
-
-## Registry and specification traceability
-
-The producer instructions identify internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md as authority because the task description's v0.5.0 pin is stale.
-
-At the Story checkpoint registry state, the decoded ownership registry binds all four leaves. All five Story-specific tmux acceptance case IDs have clause edges, checked by TestStoryV070AcceptanceCasesHaveClauseEdges and the direct decoded registry check. The task-specific clause edges are: tmux-private-server-management-v070 → 4.2#4–#7; tmux-lifecycle-operations-v070 → 4.2#9 and 4.C#3/#4/#7; tmux-attach-overlap-v070 → 4.C#6; tmux-attach-semantics-v070 → 4.C#3/#5/#6/#7; tmux-socket-custody-v070 → 3.2#8. The registry contains 159 case definitions overall; this task claim covers the five tmux Story cases. The canonical digest before the trunk-movement blocker is:
-
-276bd81b99fb924b2d94691fb2ef0687194771dfc71e294601e989f359688008
-
-The exact-tree default tracecheck passed:
-
-traceability ok: contracts=64 normative_sections=36 acceptance_cases=159 fixtures=33 compatibility_contracts=55 assigned_scopes=0
-section coverage: bindings=70 full=4 partial=10 sliver=11 unevidenced=41 unmeasured=4 unowned=7 clauses_discharged=81/585
-
-README.md measured-coverage text equals that output; TestREADMEMeasuredCoverageMatchesTracecheckReport passed on the final candidate. The Story table records 97 of 97 Story rows, including this leaf's rows 93–97.
-
-Assigned-scope checks were also rerun. These refusals are the intended closed-scope results because the tmux leaf does not own every clause in those sections:
-
-- Section 3.2: 1/13, sliver; exit 1.
-- Section 4.2: 5/11, sliver; exit 1.
-- Section 4.C: 5/7, partial; exit 1.
-- Section 4.D: 1/3, sliver; exit 1.
-- Section 4.E: no scoped implementation owner; exit 1.
-
-### Trunk movement blocker
-
-At handoff preparation, origin/main was 14d636e40fffbe8a044dcb80bb5ee28c0372f31b; the Story checkpoint and merge base were c9233ce2b7d98b70707cb3aec28f919d53a4c020. origin/main is two commits ahead of that base. Its latest ownership registry adds the landed STORY-260922-cpkajd derivation-side profile-source acceptance case and changes Section 2.4 test references.
-
-Applying only that registry delta makes the current candidate's traceability tests fail: the trunk registry refers to profile-source tests that are not present in this pinned Story tree, and TestV070RegistryRederivesFromTrunkV060Registry expects the previous trunk projection. The attempted delta and real failing output are retained in the archive. I reversed that single-file delta to keep the candidate internally consistent and tracecheck green; the outstanding operator task is to converge this managed Story workspace onto fresh trunk, carry/revalidate the uncommitted delta, then merge the current trunk registry and rederive its digest. This run cannot perform that operation: task-board documents worktree converge as an orchestrator command and refuses it for a tracked run, while this assignment forbids branch/base operations and limits source scope to production-tmux-backend.
-
-Therefore the conditional story-final registry checklist item is incomplete and the task remains blocked pending that operator convergence. Setting the task status to blocked produced task-board side effects demoting STORY-260830-2t4g7i and EPIC-260830-1uwj54 from development to integrating; the scoped query confirmed both statuses, and no manual reset was made. The exact requirement, evidence, and next action are in UNRESOLVED_QUESTIONS.md. The task handoff command was not run because its checklist precondition is not met.
-
-## Importer outcome comparison
-
-The exact base checkpoint and task candidate used the same 224-row corpus across all 36 importer packages. There are 224 shared keys, zero base-only keys, zero candidate-only keys, and one moved outcome class:
-
-| Package | Entry | Input class | Base | Candidate |
-|---|---|---|---|---|
-| tmuxserver | ServerProber.Probe | permissive-0644 | success; one Dial and one admit | tmux_unsafe_socket_path before Dial; zero Dial and zero admits |
-
-Other corpus outcomes were unchanged. The ExecuteAttachOverlapRace row is retained from the accepted predecessor corpus; TestAttachOverlapAdmissionAtomicAcrossLifecycleInstances was rerun on both base and candidate. It was not regenerated by the custom importer driver. The corrected candidate scratch tree was verified to contain the socket-custody gate; the earlier unpatched scratch attempt is excluded.
-
-## Validation
-
-All commands below were run in this task worktree; the evidence archive contains the logs and exact exit codes.
-
-- Candidate full suite: go test ./... -count=1 -v — all 45 packages passed.
-- Race sweep: five bounded package groups, all exit 0.
-- Coverage sweep: go test ./... -cover -count=1 — exit 0.
-- Configured fuzz suite: 18 targets at -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1 — all exit 0.
-- Final focused rerun after the traceability summary edit: go test ./internal/tmuxserver ./internal/traceability/... -count=1 -v — exit 0.
-- Registry clause-edge/rederivation and README pin tests passed after the final registry state was restored.
-- Default tracecheck passed after final edits; all five scoped tracecheck logs are captured in the evidence archive as expected refusals.
-- gofmt check, native and Windows vet, go build ./..., Linux and Windows builds, catalog generation, JSON parsing, and git diff --check passed.
-- Base importer package suites passed in four bounded groups; the candidate importer package group rerun exited 0. The per-test importer outcome driver covered the complete 36-package set.
-- task-board validate exited 0 and reported 256 repository-wide existing issues. A targeted search found no issue mentioning this task or Story.
-
-The final full-suite/race/coverage/fuzz runs preceded only the final documentation summary correction and trunk-registry attempt/rollback; no Go source changed afterward. The relevant tmuxserver and traceability packages, README coverage pin, registry edge/rederivation tests, and default tracecheck were rerun on the resulting exact tree.
-
-The accidental early importer log redirection outside the worktree was stopped and removed. The incident and importer scratch-tree correction are recorded under .temp/TASK-260830-g0pcnt and included in the evidence archive.
