+- NEGATIVE EVIDENCE: 14 isolated narrowing mutants were KILLED. `N-socket-permissions` preserves the `CheckSocketCustody` token while admitting a 0644 socket; the harness runs behavioral caller-entry tests, which fail before Dial/dispatch/unlink/spawn. The source-checker also has a token-preserving behavior mutant.
+- REGISTRY / TRACEABILITY: refreshed registry includes the four Story leaves and this task's decoded clause edges. `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256=3664ab2fb166189545fea34a068a318af4f251689f29c92915fa185fefdedeea`; default tracecheck reports 160 acceptance cases and `clauses_discharged=81/585`. README measured-coverage text matches. B44 remains an explicit liveness bound owned by a future authoritative receipt/protocol owner.
+- IMPORTER COMPARISON: 224 shared keys across all 36 importer packages; one moved class is `tmuxserver / ServerProber.Probe / permissive-0644`, from successful dial/admit to `tmux_unsafe_socket_path` before Dial. `ExecuteAttachOverlapRace` was retained from the accepted predecessor corpus and its named atomicity test was rerun on base and candidate.
+- VALIDATION: 45 packages passed the full suite, split race sweep, coverage sweep, and 17 configured fuzz targets. Native/Windows vet, native/Linux/Windows builds, catalog generation, JSON parsing, gofmt, traceability, and diff checks passed. Logs and the detailed outcome matrix are under `.temp/TASK-260830-g0pcnt/`.
+- BOARD: directives read through the curated task-board wrapper returned “No directives recorded” for RUN-260923-416aa6. The bare `task-board` PATH entry was an older binary and rejected the new config; the curated wrapper is used for board mutations and handoff.
+- PROCESS ANOMALY: an early importer-log redirection briefly wrote a generated file outside this worktree. It was removed and recorded in `.temp/TASK-260830-g0pcnt/workspace-guard-incident-01.md`; the final path check found it absent. No control-root file was edited directly.
